    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Excellent! The bug is fixed. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## The Problem\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` workflow file when run through the frai CLI, even though `frai-gate init --ci` worked directly.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe frai CLI's `gate` command was using Commander.js's action callback with only positional arguments, which didn't include the `--ci` flag. When delegating to frai-gate, the flag was lost.\n\n## The Fix\nChanged the action callback in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 742-756) to:\n- Extract all arguments after `gate` from `process.argv` directly\n- Pass the complete argument list (including flags) to the spawned frai-gate process\n\n## Verification\n\u2705 Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` and confirmed both files are now created:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` \u2713\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713\n\nThe workflow file contains the correct GitHub Actions configuration for running the gate on every PR.",
